	bash scripts/test_gate_s4e_next_refuses_a_parked_language_under_the_order_of_work.sh   # ~1.6s MEASURED, hermetic (its own scratch postoffice under mktemp; the live QUEUE.tsv/claims/tasks are untouched, checked by name). ⭐ WIRED 2026-09-10 (hq_P, row `snobol4-icon-postoffice-next-refuses-a-row-of-a-language-parked-by-the-order-of-work-on-mode-line-2`, CEO-489). ⛔ THE DEFECT IT HOLDS: under MODE NONET with `THE ORDER OF WORK IS ICON ONLY` on MODE line 2, `next` served hq_P a rank-0 SNOBOL4 row through the owner-cell pass. The picker's language-freeze check was present and correct; its EXTRACTOR matched exactly one spelling, `ON <LANG> ONLY`, and the ceo had written `IS ICON ONLY` -- so it returned empty, empty is documented as NO FREEZE, and every parked-language row became servable in silence. ⛔ AND THE GATE BESIDE IT COULD NOT CATCH THAT: test_gate_next_honours_the_lane_cut.sh's freeze fixture writes `ON SNOBOL4 ONLY`, the one spelling the parser knew -- the canary shared the guard's failure mode, the same shape as the argnote sweep's stale prune. ⭐ SO THIS GATE'S ARM (a) GRADES THE LIVE PROSE VERBATIM, never a fixture written to suit the parser, and it was proven RED against the pre-cure picker (4 of 10 arms) before being wired. The cure under test is a machine line the bus reads -- `ORDER-OF-WORK: <live languages>`, matched by MARKER at any depth rather than by line number, because the ceo prepends each dated entry and a positional read would silently start answering for a superseded order of work.
