SHELL := /bin/bash
preflight:  # ⭐ THE CHEAP HERMETIC ARMS, WITH NO BUILD (hq_T's ask 2026-09-06, measured by them: the Makefile had all/pristine/test/test-postoffice/buildinfo/scrip/clean and NO cheap target of any kind, so EVERY sub-second hermetic arm was trapped behind a full build -- a STRUCTURAL disincentive, not anyone's discipline). ⛔ THE MISSING `scrip` PREREQUISITE IS THE ENTIRE POINT OF THIS TARGET AND MUST NOT BE ADDED. Population DECLARED in scripts/preflight_arms.txt because a static grep cannot classify it in either direction (it convicts strip_comments.py, which says "make test" in its prose, and it clears test_gate_pl_quad_regs.sh, which reaches the compiler through a lib_ helper without naming it); scripts/test_gate_preflight_arms_stay_cheap.sh PINS EVERY ARM BY MEASURED DURATION so this cannot quietly acquire a 45-second arm and stop being worth running.
	@bad=0; n=0; \
	while read -r arm; do \
	  n=$$((n + 1)); \
	  case "$$arm" in *.py*) out=$$(cd "$(ROOT)" && python3 $$arm </dev/null 2>&1) ;; *) out=$$(cd "$(ROOT)" && bash $$arm </dev/null 2>&1) ;; esac; \
	  rc=$$?; \
	  if [ $$rc -ne 0 ]; then bad=$$((bad + 1)); printf '  RED  rc=%-3s %s\n' "$$rc" "$${arm%% *}"; printf '%s\n' "$$out" | tail -3 | sed 's/^/       /'; fi; \
	done < <(grep -E '^scripts/' "$(ROOT)/scripts/preflight_arms.txt"); \
	echo "preflight: $$n arm(s), $$bad red -- NO BUILD, hermetic. NOT a substitute for the test target: it cannot see a codegen defect."; \
	[ $$bad -eq 0 ]

test-boards:  # ⭐ THE PACKAGE BOARDS, SPLIT OUT OF `make test` 2026-09-08 (cfo, ECONOMY, on CEO-433/431 in GOAL-CEO.md): board_packages.sh runs every vendored package/third-party suite and prints the denominator (suites=/graded=/unproven=). It was the REPORTED, NOT BLOCKING arm of `make test` (MASTER-PLAN I21, D1 stage): its exit code is 0 whenever it measured, red constituent suites included, so it could never fail the build -- and it cost every seat ~10 minutes per blocking run. The coo's measure runs this target; any seat runs it on demand. D5 turns the measured floor into a real gate, and that gate goes back into `test` when it exists.
	$(MAKE) scrip
	bash scripts/board_packages.sh

test: scrip  # ⭐ WAS THE FALSE-GREEN TRAP (cured hq_P s268): `test`, `test-ir` and `test-all` were named in .PHONY with NO RECIPE ANYWHERE, so each exited 0 having run NOTHING ("Nothing to be done for 'test'") while reading as a full green suite. `test-ir` and `test-all` are DELETED rather than wired — nothing behind them ever existed. This target now runs THE blocking set named in CLAUDE.md and fails loudly on the first red. ⛔ HQ-27 PRISTINE-BEFORE-VERDICT IS VOID as a per-landing requirement (Lon 2026-09-03 ~15:58, RULES.md FACT RULE: "It's time to loosen this pristine build that keeps preventing forward progress and causes 20 minute wait times."). A landing verdict runs on an INCREMENTAL make -- never on a stale binary, and the stale-binary refusal stays as the guard. `make pristine` survives for the ceo's audits, release points, and whenever that refusal fires; the receipt names the build it graded on. This comment asserted the retired law for hours after it was retired, which is the failure mode the FACT RULE exists to prevent: law that lives in a second unversioned place cannot be retired in one edit.
	python3 scripts/strip_comments.py --check   # ~0.8s MEASURED (0.79/0.83/0.80 over three runs, 384 files), the cheapest arm here and the only one needing no build at all, so a style red fails in under a second instead of after a 6-minute board. ⭐ WIRED 2026-09-03 (hq_P, row strip-comments-check-is-not-in-make-test-so-src-style-goes-red-on-origin, minted by hq_C): RULES.md § C style -- src/ carries ZERO comments but the sanctioned 200-char /*---*/ and /*===*/ separators -- was enforced ONLY by a clause each Prolog rung's DONE-WHEN opted into BY HAND. A seat that omitted it pushed a RED gate to origin while `make test` still said green for everyone, and the redness stayed invisible until some LATER seat's DONE-WHEN ran on the merged tree. ⛔ TWICE IN ONE EVENING, hq_B's 92d300f07 and hq_P's own 84e02570, NEITHER SEAT AT FAULT in any way a reviewer would catch: a long explanatory comment is the NATURAL way to make a deletion or a shared-box change legible, and this codebase has deliberately closed that door and routed the explanation to the FINDING. A rule people must REMEMBER to copy into their own acceptance test is a hope, not a mechanism -- the same false-green shape this very target was cured of at s268.
	bash scripts/test_gate_pre_commit_refuses_a_conflict_marker.sh   # ~2s MEASURED, hermetic (scratch repos in a tempdir, no build, no network). WIRED 2026-09-06 (hq_T, ceo CEO-370 rank 1, hq_C's mint). ⛔ WHY IT SITS THIRD, beside the other two cheap arms: a conflict marker committed to a shared authority does not fail where it was made -- it fails for every OTHER seat, in a file they never touched. Measured 2026-09-06: a SCORE.md landed carrying markers, util_score_row.py could not parse the table, and THE LEADERBOARD WRITER WAS DEAD FOR AN HOUR WHILE EVERY BOARD STILL READ GREEN, because a failed row-write is non-fatal BY DESIGN (gate_score_row) so a bookkeeping failure never reds a board. Both of those decisions are right alone and compose into a hole. ⭐ This arm grades the HOOK, which is the copy that fires while the author is still present; the SCORE.md-parse arm is the second half and catches what already landed. ⛔ It also grades that the INSTALLED hook matches scripts/lib_pre_commit_hook.txt in all three repos -- hooks do not propagate through clone, so a cured hook in one root protects one root.
	bash scripts/test_gate_score_md_parses_and_github_is_marker_free.sh   # ~1s MEASURED, no build. WIRED 2026-09-06 (hq_T, ceo CEO-370 rank 1, minted from hq_R's blocker). THE LANDING-TIME HALF of the arm above: the pre-commit hook grades the commit in front of it in the root where it is installed, and HOOKS DO NOT PROPAGATE THROUGH CLONE -- it cannot see what already reached origin, a --no-verify, or a seat whose hook was never installed. ⛔ THE INCIDENT: a SCORE.md landed with markers, util_score_row.py could not find its table, and the leaderboard writer was DEAD FOR AN HOUR while every board read GREEN. Neither component is at fault -- gate_score_row is non-fatal BY DESIGN so a bookkeeping failure never reds a board, which is right, and a corrupt shared file is invisible to a board, which is expected. THE HOLE IS THE COMPOSITION, and this arm is the distinction made mechanical: a failed WRITE must not red a board, a corrupt LEADERBOARD must. ⭐ TWO VERDICTS ON PURPOSE: rc=2 when the table cannot be read (this gate cannot measure, so it refuses rather than inventing a verdict -- an unparseable board is not a failing board) and rc=1 for a marker in a tracked .github file, which IS a defect. Both proven by ablation.
	bash scripts/test_gate_raku_paren_call_passes_its_arguments.sh   # ~3s MEASURED (2.9/3.1/3.0), no oracle and no network: A PARENTHESIZED RAKU CALL PASSES ITS ARGUMENTS, never one concatenated list. ⭐ WIRED 2026-09-06 (hq_T, CEO-332 / Lon: "let's not see stuck ever again ... go fix ONE program in each and let's begin the climb") -- the gate under the cure that flipped roast S04-statements/until.t, the first Roast program to go green since 09-03. ⛔ WHY A GATE AND NOT A BOARD LINE: the broken form still emitted VALID TAP -- plan, four well-formed `not ok` lines, rc=0 -- and the only evidence was three arguments concatenated inside a diagnostic string. A whole-file board can say 986 to 985 and can never name the CALL FORM. ⭐ THE ARMS ARE DIFFERENTIAL, so they need no hand-authored expectation that could have been written to match the buggy output: f(a,b,c) and f a,b,c are the same program in Raku, so any divergence is a defect without anyone deciding which side is right -- plus one ABSOLUTE arity arm, because a purely differential gate is satisfiable by breaking BOTH forms. FAIL-ONCE PROVEN by rebuilding the pre-cure tree: 11 of 12 arms red, both modes, until.t at 0 ok / 4 not ok.
